==French==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|fr}} {{term|savon|lang=frm}}, from {{etyl|fro|fr}} {{term|savon||soap|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|LL.|fr}} {{term|sapo|sāpō|soap|lang=la}}, from Old {{etyl|frk|fr}} {{recons|saipa|saipa|soap|lang=frk}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|fr}} {{recons|saipōn||soap|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|fr}} {{recons|seib-|lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|seip-||to pour out, drip, strain, trickle|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognate with {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|sape|sāpe|soap|lang=ang}}. More at {{l|en|soap}}.

